-### Guardrail Layer Details
-
-#### Layer 1 — Input Validation (`collector/models.py`)
-
-Every event arriving from the browser at `POST /collect` is validated by a strict **Pydantic v2** schema before anything touches the database.
-
-| Check | Rule | Failure Behaviour |
-|---|---|---|
-| `event_id` | `min_length=8` | HTTP 422 — request rejected |
-| `event_type` | Must be in `ALLOWED_EVENT_TYPES` | HTTP 422 — request rejected |
-| `duration_ms` | `≥ 0` | HTTP 422 — request rejected |
-| `url` | Query string & fragment stripped | Silent sanitisation (PII removal) |
-| `metadata` | Dict or parseable JSON string; else `{}` | Silent coercion to safe default |
-| `EventBatch` | 1–100 events per request | HTTP 422 — empty or oversized batch rejected |
-| Unknown fields | `extra = "ignore"` | Silently dropped |
-
-#### Layer 2 — Pre-LLM PII Sanitiser (`guardrails/sanitiser.py`)
-
-Before any friction-score data is sent to the LLM for root-cause analysis, the `sanitise_for_llm()` function **strips all personally identifiable fields** from the dict.
+### 4. Dashboard
 
-```python
-BLOCKED_FIELDS = {"user_id", "session_id", "ip_address", "email", "verbatim", "event_id"}
-```
+`cji-dashboard`, then choose "Live_event track", "tracking_event track" or "demo_events track" in the
+sidebar.
 
-Only anonymised aggregate signals (drop-off rate, error rate, dwell time, rage-clicks, retries) are included in the prompt. This ensures the LLM never receives raw user IDs or session tokens.
